  ('mercuryo', 'Mercuryo', 'monetary-access-rails', 'global-on-ramps', 'https://mercuryo.io', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "Mercuryo is a global fiat-to-crypto on-ramp that enables users and applications to convert fiat into Ethereum assets via cards, bank transfers, and local payment methods, with a strong focus on embedded Web3 payments and wallet integrations.", "extras": {"Access Bottleneck Type": "Banking + Card Networks + Regulation", "Conversion Control Model": "Centralized", "Custody of Funds": "Temporary in-flow custody; assets delivered to user wallets", "Decentralization Impact": "Increases Ethereum accessibility while introducing centralized compliance and payment-rail dependencies", "Ethereum Support": "Ethereum Mainnet; select Ethereum L2s depending on integration", "Failure Mode": "Fiat access suspended; payment rails disabled in affected regions", "Founded Year": "2018", "Freeze / Denial Capability": "Yes", "Geographic Coverage": "Global", "Headquarters / Primary Jurisdiction": "United Kingdom / European Union (global operations)", "Is Ethereum Required for Core Function?": "Partial (multi-chain support; Ethereum is a primary destination)", "KYC / AML Requirement": "Mandatory; tiered based on transaction size and payment method", "Maintaining Organization": "Mercuryo Ltd.", "Number of Countries Supported": "100+ (approx.)", "On-Ramp vs Exchange Bias": "Access-First", "Practitioner Validation Check": "Is this entity’s primary value proposition enabling users to get fiat value into Ethereum-native assets? Yes", "Practitioner’s Note": "Mercuryo sits between consumer-facing on-ramps and backend infrastructure: broad asset support and payment optionality are strengths, while reliance on card networks and banking partners introduces familiar centralized choke points.", "Primary Dependency Risks": "Banking partners, card networks, regulatory enforcement", "Primary Function": "Fiat → Crypto Access", "Primary Regulatory Jurisdictions": "