  ('onramper', 'Onramper', 'monetary-access-rails', 'global-on-ramps', 'https://onramper.com', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "Onramper is a global on-ramp aggregator that routes users to multiple fiat-to-crypto providers, optimizing for price, payment method availability, and geographic coverage to facilitate access to Ethereum assets.", "extras": {"Access Bottleneck Type": "Partner Availability + Pricing + Regulation (inherited)", "Conversion Control Model": "Partner-Dependent", "Custody of Funds": "None (routes users to third-party on-ramps; no fiat custody)", "Decentralization Impact": "Improves access resilience and choice while adding an orchestration dependency layer", "Ethereum Support": "Ethereum Mainnet; Ethereum L2s (dependent on underlying on-ramps)", "Failure Mode": "Routing unavailable; reduced access options; degraded UX", "Founded Year": "2020", "Freeze / Denial Capability": "Indirect (via underlying on-ramp providers)", "Geographic Coverage": "Global", "Headquarters / Primary Jurisdiction": "United Kingdom (global operations)", "Is Ethereum Required for Core Function?": "Partial (multi-chain support; Ethereum is a primary destination)", "KYC / AML Requirement": "Mandatory (performed by underlying on-ramp providers)", "Maintaining Organization": "Onramper Ltd.", "Number of Countries Supported": "150+ (approx., via aggregated providers)", "On-Ramp vs Exchange Bias": "Access-First (Meta / Aggregation Layer)", "Practitioner Validation Check": "Is this entity’s primary value proposition enabling users to get fiat value into Ethereum-native assets? Yes", "Practitioner’s Note": "Onramper reduces single-provider dependency and improves conversion success rates, but introduces second-order dependency risk: access quality and reliability are inherited from the underlying on-ramps it aggregates.", "Primary Dependency Risks": "Availability and pricing of integrated on-ramps; partner outages", "Primary Function": "Fiat → Crypto Access Aggregation", "Primary Regulatory Jurisdictions": "Inherited from integrated providers (MoonPay, Ramp, Transak, etc.)", "Primary Use Case": "On-ramp aggregation; cost, coverage, and success-rate optimization", "Primary User Segment": "Wallets, dApps, and users seeking best-price fiat access", "Primary Value Flow": "Fiat → (Partner On-Ramp) → ETH / Stablecoin → Ethereum", "Reason for Inclusion": "Onramper qualifies as a Global On-Ramp because its primary value proposition is enabling fiat → Ethereum access at global scale by aggregating and orchestrating multiple on-ramp providers, even though it does not directly process fiat itself.", "Regional Restrictions": "Yes (inherits restrictions from underlying on-ramps)", "Regulatory Model": "Partner-Licensed (does not directly custody or process fiat)", "Role Relative to Ethereum": "Access Orchestration Layer / Meta-On-Ramp", "Supported Crypto Assets": "ETH, major stablecoins (USDC, USDT), partner-supported assets", "Supported Fiat Currencies": "USD, EUR, GBP, and numerous local currencies (via partners)", "Supported Payment Methods": "Cards, Bank Transfers, Local Payment Rails (via integrated on-ramps)", "Systemic Importance to Ethereum Access": "Medium"}, "source_label": "Global On-Ramps"}'::jsonb),
