  ('socket-fiat-chain-routing', 'Socket (Fiat → Chain Routing)', 'monetary-access-rails', 'global-on-ramps', 'https://www.socket.tech', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "Socket provides a chain-aware routing layer that orchestrates fiat-to-crypto onboarding by directing users through integrated on-ramps and bridging paths to land assets directly on the target Ethereum chain or L2.", "extras": {"Access Bottleneck Type": "Partner Availability + Routing Logic + Regulation (inherited)", "Conversion Control Model": "Partner-Dependent", "Custody of Funds": "None (routes users to third-party on-ramps; no fiat custody)", "Decentralization Impact": "Improves access efficiency and L2 adoption while adding an orchestration dependency layer", "Ethereum Support": "Ethereum Mainnet; Ethereum L2s (Arbitrum, Optimism, Base, Polygon)", "Failure Mode": "Fiat routing unavailable; degraded success rates or higher costs", "Founded Year": "2021", "Freeze / Denial Capability": "Indirect (via underlying on-ramp providers)", "Geographic Coverage": "Global (inherits coverage from integrated providers)", "Headquarters / Primary Jurisdiction": "United States (global operations)", "Is Ethereum Required for Core Function?": "Partial (multi-chain router; Ethereum and L2s are primary destinations)", "KYC / AML Requirement": "Mandatory (performed by underlying on-ramp providers)", "Maintaining Organization": "Socket Technologies", "Number of Countries Supported": "150+ (approx., partner-dependent)", "On-Ramp vs Exchange Bias": "Access-First (Orchestration / Routing Layer)", "Practitioner Validation Check": "Is this entity’s primary value proposition (for this use case) enabling users to get fiat value into Ethereum-native assets? Yes", "Practitioner’s Note": "Socket reduces post-onboarding friction by collapsing fiat purchase, bridging, and chain selection into a single flow, but introduces second-order dependency risk tied to partner availability and routing correctness.", "Primary Dependency Risks": "Availability, pricing, and uptime of integrated on-ramps; routing logic failures", "Primary Function": "Fiat → Crypto Access Orchestration (Routing Layer)", "Primary Regulatory Jurisdictions": "Inherited from integrated providers (MoonPay, Ramp, Transak, Coinbase On-Ramp, etc.)", "Primary Use Case": "Chain-aware fiat onboarding; routing to optimal Ethereum L2", "Primary User Segment": "Wallets, dApps, and users optimizing cost and destination chain", "Primary Value Flow": "Fiat → (Partner On-Ramp) → Stablecoin / ETH → Target Ethereum Chain", "Reason for Inclusion": "Socket qualifies as a Global On-Ramp because, when used for fiat → chain routing, its primary value proposition is enabling users to enter Ethereum and its L2s efficiently, even though it does not directly process fiat.", "Regional Restrictions": "Yes (inherits jurisdictional limits from underlying on-ramps)", "Regulatory Model": "Partner-Licensed (does not directly custody or process fiat)", "Role Relative to Ethereum": "Access Orchestration Layer (Chain-Aware Router)", "Supported Crypto Assets": "ETH, major stablecoins (USDC, USDT), partner-supported assets", "Supported Fiat Currencies": "USD, EUR, GBP, and local currencies (via integrated on-ramps)", "Supported Payment Methods": "Cards, Bank Transfers, Local Payment Rails (via partners)", "Systemic Importance to Ethereum Access": "Medium"}, "source_label": "Global On-Ramps"}'::jsonb),
