lly idiosyncratic: it dominates institutional settlement volume on Ethereum while introducing elevated issuer, regulatory, and banking-partner risk compared to fully regulated peers.", "Primary Dependency Risks": "Banking partners, regulatory enforcement, reserve transparency, issuer risk", "Primary Function": "Institutional stablecoin settlement; treasury and cross-border value transfer", "Primary Regulatory Jurisdictions": "BVI; compliance interfaces in U.S., EU, Asia via partners", "Primary Use Case": "High-value settlement, exchange liquidity provisioning, cross-border treasury flows", "Programmability Level": "Static Payments (limited programmability at issuer level)", "Reason for Inclusion": "Tether qualifies as an Institutional Payment Rail because USDT on Ethereum is extensively used for large-scale, institutional settlement flows where Ethereum provides the final settlement layer, even when operational processes are abstracted.", "Regulatory Posture": "Offshore / Partner-Regulated (jurisdictionally fragmented)", "Settlement Asset Types": "Stablecoins (USDT)", "Settlement vs Access Classification": "Settlement Rail", "Systemic Importance to Ethereum": "High", "Target User Segment": "Exchanges, market makers, OTC desks, enterprises, fintechs", "Transaction Scale": "High-value and high-volume"}, "source_label": "Institutional Payment Rails"}'::jsonb),
